title: Scroll Position Memory
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
modified: 20260803194150209

When you scroll within a long tiddler, the plugin waits until scrolling settles and then remembers how deep you are. Navigating to that tiddler again restores the position instead of showing its top.

Positions are only remembered beyond a minimum depth (100 pixels by default, see [[Settings]]), and only for tiddlers taller than the browser window. Scrolling back to the top of a tiddler clears its memory again.

To see it work: this tiddler is short, so it has no position memory. Go back to the long [[Scroll Memory Documentation]], scroll somewhere into its middle, open any other tiddler, and then navigate to the documentation again. You arrive exactly where you were.
